WEBVTT

00:00:05.052 --> 00:00:06.531
[ whimpers]

00:00:06.575 --> 00:00:07.924
[ panting]

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:09.099
[ roars]

00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:11.928
[ yelps, growling]

00:00:11.971 --> 00:00:14.365
[ howls]

00:00:14.409 --> 00:00:15.758
What are you doing?

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:16.976
Saving your life!

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.022
[ howls]

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:20.545
[ snarls]

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:23.244
HARRY:
Thanks.

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:24.462
[ growling]

00:00:24.506 --> 00:00:25.637
Great! Now he's
coming for us.

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:28.466
Yeah, I didn't think
about that. Run!

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:29.554
[ whining]

00:00:29.598 --> 00:00:32.470
[ panting]

00:00:36.126 --> 00:00:37.954
[ whining]

00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:40.478
[ vicious snarling]

00:00:42.132 --> 00:00:43.264
[ panting]

00:00:43.307 --> 00:00:44.265
[ grunts]

00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:45.266
[ gasps]

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:48.921
[ panting]

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:51.837
[ distant whining]

00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:56.929
[ growls]

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:59.106
[ panting]

00:01:01.456 --> 00:01:04.067
[ low growls]

00:01:04.111 --> 00:01:06.591
[ snarls]

00:01:08.158 --> 00:01:12.336
[ howls]

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.299
[ panting]

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.652
[ low growling]

00:01:23.695 --> 00:01:25.436
[ gasps]

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.959
[ snarling]

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:28.657
[ screams]
[ roars]

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.049
[ cawing]

00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:31.834
[ snarling]

00:01:31.877 --> 00:01:35.011
[ cawing]

00:01:35.054 --> 00:01:37.492
[ yelping]

00:01:37.535 --> 00:01:40.321
[ bellowing]

00:01:44.325 --> 00:01:45.935
[ gasping]:
That was so scary.

00:01:45.978 --> 00:01:49.765
Poor Professor Lupin's
having a really tough night.

00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:52.855
[ rustling]

00:01:52.898 --> 00:01:56.598
[ clock ticking]

00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:01.385
Sirius.

00:02:01.429 --> 00:02:03.605
Come on!

00:02:13.919 --> 00:02:15.878
[ screeching]

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:19.142
[ gurgling groans]

00:02:19.186 --> 00:02:20.317
This is horrible.

00:02:20.361 --> 00:02:22.537
Don't worry.
My dad will come.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.670
He'll conjure
the Patronus.

00:02:26.932 --> 00:02:30.371
[ screeching]

00:02:30.632 --> 00:02:32.547
[ gurgling groans]

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.245
Any minute now!

00:02:35.289 --> 00:02:36.812
Right there!
You'll see!

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:38.509
[ screeching continues]

00:02:38.553 --> 00:02:40.250
Harry,
listen to me.

00:02:40.294 --> 00:02:41.556
No one's coming.

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:43.035
Don't worry!
He will!

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:44.167
He will come!

00:02:44.211 --> 00:02:45.821
[ gurgling gasps, grunts]

00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:47.605
[ disembodied screech]

00:02:47.649 --> 00:02:48.954
HARRY:
Sirius?

00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:51.870
HERMIONE:
You're dying...

00:02:52.784 --> 00:02:55.439
...both of you.

00:02:56.614 --> 00:02:59.095
Harry!

00:03:00.401 --> 00:03:03.447
Expecto Patronum!

00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:05.623
[ distorted hum]

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.756
[ panting]

00:03:19.246 --> 00:03:21.900
[ panting]

00:03:23.293 --> 00:03:27.123
[ weak, muffled screeching]

00:03:30.431 --> 00:03:35.218
[ intermittent whooshing hum]

00:03:37.438 --> 00:03:40.571
[ panting]

00:03:43.444 --> 00:03:46.229
[ ground crunching]

00:03:49.537 --> 00:03:51.582
[ hum fades]

00:03:51.626 --> 00:03:55.151
[ panting]

00:04:03.028 --> 00:04:04.421
You were right, Hermione.

00:04:04.465 --> 00:04:06.554
It wasn't my dad
I saw earlier.

00:04:06.597 --> 00:04:08.033
It was me.

00:04:08.077 --> 00:04:10.558
I saw myself conjuring
the Patronus before.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:13.343
I knew I could
do it this time, because...

00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:15.345
well, I'd already done it.

00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:16.651
Does that make sense?

00:04:16.694 --> 00:04:18.000
No!

00:04:18.043 --> 00:04:19.393
But I don't like fly...

00:04:19.436 --> 00:04:21.003
[ screaming]

00:04:21.046 --> 00:04:22.874
HARRY:
Whoo-hoo!

00:04:34.277 --> 00:04:35.931
Bombarda!

00:04:36.366 --> 00:04:43.939
[ Sirius laughing]

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:47.638
Whoo!

00:04:47.682 --> 00:04:51.381
[ whooping]

00:05:04.612 --> 00:05:07.528
[ chirruping]

00:05:08.572 --> 00:05:11.009
I'll be forever
grateful for this.

00:05:11.053 --> 00:05:12.837
To both of you.

00:05:12.881 --> 00:05:14.404
I want to go with you.

00:05:14.448 --> 00:05:15.710
One day,
perhaps.

00:05:15.753 --> 00:05:16.841
For some time,

00:05:16.885 --> 00:05:18.495
my life will be
too unpredictable.

00:05:18.539 --> 00:05:21.237
And besides...

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.805
you're meant
to be here.

00:05:23.848 --> 00:05:25.241
But you're innocent.

00:05:25.284 --> 00:05:27.330
And you know it.

00:05:27.374 --> 00:05:29.724
And for now, that'll do.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.378
HERMIONE:
Down, Buckbeak.

00:05:31.421 --> 00:05:33.423
I expect
you're tired

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.034
of hearing this...

00:05:36.078 --> 00:05:39.603
but you look
so like your father.

00:05:40.952 --> 00:05:42.389
Except your eyes.

00:05:42.432 --> 00:05:43.564
You have...

00:05:43.607 --> 00:05:45.348
My mother's eyes.

00:05:45.392 --> 00:05:47.002
[ chuckles]

00:05:47.045 --> 00:05:48.569
It's cruel

00:05:48.612 --> 00:05:50.484
that I got to spend so much time
with James and Lily

00:05:50.527 --> 00:05:52.964
and you so little.

00:05:53.008 --> 00:05:54.618
But know this...

00:05:54.662 --> 00:05:58.448
the ones that love us
never really leave us.

00:05:58.492 --> 00:06:04.454
And you can
always find them...

00:06:04.498 --> 00:06:07.414
in here.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.597
[ chirruping]

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.514
You really are the brightest
witch of your age.

00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:28.130
[ reverberating call]

00:06:43.754 --> 00:06:46.322
[ bell tolling]

00:06:46.365 --> 00:06:48.890
We have to go!

00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:10.041
[ clicking, creaking]

00:07:10.085 --> 00:07:15.656
[ panting]

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:16.831
Well?

00:07:16.874 --> 00:07:19.790
He's free.
We did it.

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:20.835
Did what?

00:07:20.878 --> 00:07:22.489
Good night.

00:07:22.532 --> 00:07:25.666
[ humming]

00:07:31.802 --> 00:07:33.195
How did you get there?

00:07:33.238 --> 00:07:34.631
You were... I was
talking to you there.

00:07:34.675 --> 00:07:35.980
[ whimpers]:
And now you're there.

00:07:36.024 --> 00:07:37.895
What's he talking
about, Harry?

00:07:37.939 --> 00:07:39.331
I don't know.

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:40.768
Honestly, Ron,

00:07:40.811 --> 00:07:42.465
how can somebody be in
two places at once?

00:07:42.509 --> 00:07:44.554
[ chuckling]

00:07:44.598 --> 00:07:48.645
[ bird chirping]

00:07:48.689 --> 00:07:50.560
[ thuds]

00:07:50.604 --> 00:07:55.870
[ creaking]

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:08.622
[ music playing]

00:08:08.665 --> 00:08:11.276
LUPIN:
Hello, Harry.

00:08:14.236 --> 00:08:17.587
I saw you coming.

00:08:19.937 --> 00:08:25.290
I've looked worse, believe me.

00:08:26.117 --> 00:08:27.292
You've been sacked.

00:08:27.336 --> 00:08:31.383
No. No.
I resigned, actually.

00:08:31.427 --> 00:08:33.560
Resigned? Why?

00:08:33.603 --> 00:08:35.736
Well, it seems
that somebody

00:08:35.779 --> 00:08:38.956
let slip the nature
of my condition.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.567
This time tomorrow,

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.959
the owls will
start arriving

00:08:42.003 --> 00:08:45.006
and parents will
not want a, um...

00:08:45.049 --> 00:08:49.140
well, someone like me
teaching their children.

00:08:49.184 --> 00:08:50.315
But Dumbledore...

00:08:50.359 --> 00:08:51.882
Dumbledore
has already risked

00:08:51.926 --> 00:08:53.231
enough on my behalf.

00:08:53.275 --> 00:08:55.190
Besides, people
like me are, um....

00:08:55.233 --> 00:09:01.239
Well, let's just say that
I'm used to it by now.

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:08.899
[ music playing ends]

00:09:08.943 --> 00:09:11.641
Why do you look
so miserable, Harry?

00:09:11.685 --> 00:09:14.470
None of it
made any difference.

00:09:14.513 --> 00:09:16.385
Pettigrew escaped.

00:09:16.428 --> 00:09:18.213
Didn't make any difference?

00:09:18.256 --> 00:09:20.302
Harry, it made all the
difference in the world.

00:09:20.345 --> 00:09:21.869
You helped
uncover the truth.

00:09:21.912 --> 00:09:24.785
You saved an innocent
man from a terrible fate.

00:09:24.828 --> 00:09:27.526
It made a great
deal of difference.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.051
[ groans]

00:09:30.094 --> 00:09:33.881
If I am proud of anything,

00:09:33.924 --> 00:09:36.797
it is of how much
you have learned this year.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.408
Now, since I am
no longer your teacher,

00:09:39.451 --> 00:09:44.805
I feel no guilt, whatsoever,
about giving this back to you.

00:09:44.848 --> 00:09:47.808
So now I'll say
good-bye, Harry.

00:09:47.851 --> 00:09:51.289
I feel sure we'll
meet again sometime.

00:09:51.333 --> 00:09:53.596
Until then...

00:09:54.205 --> 00:09:56.643
...mischief managed.

00:09:58.601 --> 00:10:01.691
[ chuckles]

